    "main_topic": [
      {
        "h_title": "Lod Chong Thai",
        "main_title": "Lod Chong Thai",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 1,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Just about anywhere in Thailand you'll find a street vendor specializing in sweets, and Lod Chong is probably the most popular of Thai sweets so all of these vendors will have it. A strange sight for the newcomer to Lod Chong, it looks like little green worms in icy sugary water. A lovely combination of bright green color, rich sugary flavor, earthy fragrance and stomach-filling rice pasta. A must for anyone traveling to Thailand.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": [
          {
            "text": "You might also be interested in our Street Vendor Video: How to Make Lod Chong",
            "url": "http://importfood.com/videos/Lod-Chong-Thai-Video.html",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "http://importfood.com/videos/Lod-Chong-Thai-Video.html",
                "anchor_text": "Street Vendor Video: How to Make Lod Chong"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Also of interest: Lod Chong Singapore",
            "url": "http://importfood.com/videos/Lod-Chong-Singapore-Video.html",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "http://importfood.com/videos/Lod-Chong-Singapore-Video.html",
                "anchor_text": "Lod Chong Singapore"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "To make this, you will need a Lod Chong Press",
            "url": "http://importfood.com/thai-cookware/lod-chong-press.html",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "http://importfood.com/thai-cookware/lod-chong-press.html",
                "anchor_text": "Lod Chong Press"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Method",
        "main_title": "Lod Chong Thai",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 4,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Pour rice flour in a large wok, followed by mung bean flour and the pandan water mixture. Cook over medium heat.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Start to stir right away. The recommended technique is to stir in one direction only. Continue stirring for 10-15 minutes until the batter starts to set with thick consistency.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Turn off the heat and pour the cooked batter into a Lod Chong press with a bucket below containing water at room temperature to capture the Lod Chong noodles. Press down in a pumping motion so the noodles will be short.",
            "url": "http://importfood.com/thai-cookware/lod-chong-press.html",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "http://importfood.com/thai-cookware/lod-chong-press.html",
                "anchor_text": "Lod Chong press"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Pandan Water: Prepare slaked lime water by mixing two tablespoons lime paste, then squeeze the leaves & strain until you get fragrant, green water.",
            "url": "http://importfood.com/lime_paste.html",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "http://importfood.com/lime_paste.html",
                "anchor_text": "lime paste, then squeeze the leaves & strain until you get fragrant, green water."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "See our Video: How To Make Lod Chong Thai",
            "url": "http://importfood.com/videos/Lod-Chong-Thai-Video.html",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "http://importfood.com/videos/Lod-Chong-Thai-Video.html",
                "anchor_text": "How To Make Lod Chong Thai"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Topping Sauce",
        "main_title": "Lod Chong Thai",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 4,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "In a pot, melt the palm sugar and jasmine water together. When it comes to a boil, remove it from heat and stir in the sugar right away. Add coconut cream and sir until blended.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      }
    ],
